---
description: Next.js 16 App Router conventions
globs: apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# RSC vs Client
- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for: state, effects, event handlers, browser-only libs (charts, d3, Mantine portals).
- Fetch in Server Components with the SDK; pass serializable props to client children.
- Long-running reads go through `<Suspense>` with streaming; no global loading spinners in RSC trees.

# Routing
- Use route groups `(app)` / `(marketing)` for layout separation (already present).
- Prefer parallel routes for dashboards with independent panes.
- Route handlers (`app/api/**/route.ts`) are BFF only — no business logic; proxy to `apps/api` SDK.

# Caching
- Use `fetch` cache tags + `revalidateTag` after mutations instead of `router.refresh()` unless UX requires it.
- Do not disable caching globally; opt-out per request with `cache: 'no-store'` when data is user-specific.

# Do not
- Do not import server-only code (`env.ts`, SDK server bindings) from a `"use client"` file.
- Do not call `cookies()`/`headers()` outside Server Components or route handlers.
